<Base title="About" description="Why Order of Movies exists, how we choose between release and chronological order, and how the site makes money.">
  <div class="wrap"><section class="section prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Order of Movies exists to answer one question quickly: what do I watch, and in what order?</p>
    <p>Every franchise here is laid out twice. <strong>Release order</strong> is how audiences originally saw it — usually the best way to protect twists and watch a series find its feet. <strong>Chronological order</strong> follows the story's own timeline, which is often tidier and occasionally ruins something.</p>
    <p>Where the two disagree, we say which we'd pick and why. We'd rather take a position than list both and leave you to it.</p>
    <h2>How we make money</h2>
    <p>Some of the "Where to watch" and "Buy" links earn a commission if you use them. It costs you nothing and it has no bearing on what we recommend — the orders are the orders.</p>
    <h2>Spotted a mistake?</h2>
    <p>Timelines get retconned and new films shuffle old ones. If something here is wrong, tell us and we'll fix it.</p>
  </section></div>
</Base>
